      "content": "While I can understand your desire to take full advantage of your investment in the office chair, it's important to adhere to proper accounting practices. An expensive ergonomic chair can typically be written off as a business expense in the year it was purchased if it's expected to last more than a year. If your accountant approves it as an immediate deduction, you can classify it as a Section 179 Deduction or an immediate expensing business expense under the IRS rules, but you should definitely consult your accountant or review with the IRS guidelines for proper tax treatment based on your specific situation. Always ensure you're following the IRS guidelines and making sure it meets your business's accounting practices.",
